  look like /#/basic-rules. Search engines ignore the #fragment, which means
  only the root URL is a distinct, indexable page today. Per-section indexing
  requires switching the router to history mode (createWebHistory) + an SPA
  fallback on the bucket/CDN — once that's done, list each section here.

  Until then we expose the only two real, distinct URLs: the EN root and its
  ?lang=ru language variant (see hreflang in index.html / useLocale.js).
-->
